  "Question": "Plan A has a monthly fee of 30 yuan plus 0.1 yuan/minute; Plan B has no monthly fee and charges 0.15 yuan/minute. If someone makes 500 minutes of calls per month, which plan saves more money?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "Plan A costs less",
    "B": "Plan B costs less",
    "C": "The two plans cost the same"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Plan A: \\(30+0.1\\times500=80\\) yuan; Plan B: \\(0.15\\times500=75\\) yuan. Plan B costs less. (The two plans cost the same when \\(30+0.1t=0.15t\\), giving \\(t=600\\). Plan B costs less for fewer than 600 minutes of calls.)\n\nAlternative method 1: Compare the fee with the call savings\n\nPlan A saves \\(0.15-0.10=0.05\\) yuan per minute in call charges. Over \\(500\\) minutes, this saves \\(0.05\\times500=25\\) yuan. Its monthly fee is \\(30\\) yuan, which exceeds these savings by \\(30-25=5\\) yuan. Therefore, Plan B costs \\(5\\) yuan less. Choose B.",
